meta {
  name: Get Course Scholarship Details
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/colleges/by-slug/{{collegeSlug}}/courses/{{courseId}}/scholarship-details?port_entry_id=port_jee_main&score_range_id=range_1-1000
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  port_entry_id: port_jee_main
  score_range_id: range_1-1000
}

docs {
  Dedicated endpoint for the Merit Scholarship calculator on a course's
  Financial Aid tab — NOT the same as the generic GET
  .../courses/:courseId/tabs/financial_aid endpoint. That generic route
  returns the full raw/transformed tab (including financial_concessions).
  This endpoint resolves just the scholarship calculator's criteria/discount
  for a specific Port of Entry + Score Range selection.

  Path params:
  - collegeSlug: College subdomain slug
  - courseId: Course ID

  Query params (both optional):
  - port_entry_id: a port entry `id` from the `port_entries` array below
  - score_range_id: a score range `id` nested under that port entry's
    `score_ranges` array

  `port_entries` is ALWAYS the full, unfiltered list — every port entry,
  each with its OWN nested `score_ranges` array (not flattened). It does not
  change based on the query params. This lets the frontend render the full
  port-entry → score-range hierarchy from a single no-filter call, with no
  round-trip needed after picking a port entry.

  `details` is ONLY resolved once a real selection is made:
  - no filter (or invalid/incomplete filter) → details is null
  - port_entry_id valid AND score_range_id valid (within that port entry's
    score_ranges) → details resolves to that score range's discount/amounts,
    with `criteria` being the selected port entry's terms_and_conditions list

  Response (no filter):
  {
    "port_entries": [
      {
        "id": "port_college_entrance_exam",
        "name": "College Entrance Exam",
        "score_ranges": [
          { "id": "range_90_100", "range_label": "90-100" },
          { "id": "range_75_90", "range_label": "75-90" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "port_jee",
        "name": "JEE",
        "score_ranges": [
          { "id": "range_50_100", "range_label": "50-100" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "details": null,
    "filters_applied": { "port_entry_id": null, "score_range_id": null }
  }

  Response (with a valid filter):
  {
    "port_entries": [...],
    "details": {
      "criteria": ["minimum 45% score", "minimum 60% +2 score"],
      "discount_type": "amount",
      "discount_value": 10000,
      "max_scholarship_amount": "₹10,000",
      "net_payable_amount": "₹2,30,000"
    },
    "filters_applied": {
      "port_entry_id": "port_college_entrance_exam",
      "score_range_id": "range_90_100"
    }
  }

  `filters_applied` echoes back exactly what was resolved (both null when
  nothing was selected or selection didn't match anything real). All text
  fields are trimmed of leading/trailing whitespace; criteria lines also
  collapse any embedded newlines into spaces.

  Response message: "Scholarship details fetched successfully".
  Returns 404 "Course not found" if the course/college doesn't exist or
  isn't active.

  Table: courses (metadata JSONB, tabData.financial_aid.merit_scholarship)
}
